     1	# Cycle 016 Implementation Log — Canvas presentation read ports and overlay interaction boundary
     2	
     3	## Wave 016 status
     4	
     5	**WAVE 016 COMPLETE.** The implementation and independent closure verification are green. The selected direct proposal was implemented without source broadening, all mandatory validation gates have current stable logs, and the live preview has been refreshed on `0.0.0.0:5173` with a reachability probe and focused overlay/canvas browser evidence.
     6	
     7	## Selected path and scope
     8	
     9	Implemented the decision-selected direct path from `proposal-direct.md`. No restructure/shared presentation snapshot layer was introduced. The work stayed within the decision-authorized canvas presentation, overlay boundary, focused tests, validation, and implementation-log surfaces.
    10	
    11	## Source files changed
    12	
    13	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts` — added the narrow canvas read port and `createCanvasWorldReadPort(world)` adapter. The selector/controller consume this port instead of accepting a concrete full `World` API.
    14	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/Projected3DCanvasSelector.ts` — moved projected 3D-on-2D render DTO construction out of `CanvasPresentationSelector` into a named adapter.
    15	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationController.ts` — changed `buildModel` to accept `CanvasWorldReadPort`.
    16	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationSelector.ts` — changed `select` to accept `CanvasWorldReadPort`, removed `any` helper signatures and the inline `projected3D` loop, typed arc-geometry access, and kept 2D traversal/style/query ownership local.
    17	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasVisibilityPolicy.ts` — narrowed the visibility dependency to a read-only process-tree capability used by the read port.
    18	- `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue` — wraps the injected runtime `World` with `createCanvasWorldReadPort(world)` at the canvas presentation boundary; existing tool/command interactions remain unchanged and in scope.
    19	- `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` — deleted the unused mutable `Paper` collection/query state and stale `HitResult`, leaving only primitive/style/viewport DTO types used by renderers.
    20	- `frontend/src/App.vue` — made the 3D overlay container explicitly non-intercepting (`pointer-events: none`) and added `data-testid="three-view-overlay"` for live/e2e evidence.
    21	- `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue` — made `.three-controls` explicitly interactive (`pointer-events: auto`) so overlay controls retain intentional input ownership.
    22	- `frontend/tests/unit/application/canvasPresentation/canvasPresentationSelector.spec.ts` — replaced obsolete concrete-World selector use with read-port selection.
    23	- `frontend/tests/unit/application/canvasPresentation/canvasWorldReadPort.spec.ts` — added focused read-port/controller boundary tests and compile-time guard against concrete-World selector/controller APIs.
    24	- `frontend/tests/unit/application/canvasPresentation/projected3DCanvasSelector.spec.ts` — added focused adapter coverage for projected 3D-on-2D DTO ownership.
    25	- `frontend/tests/unit/tools/pointTool.spec.ts`, `frontend/tests/unit/tools/CircleTool.spec.ts`, `frontend/tests/unit/tools/toolValidation.spec.ts` — updated existing live interaction-query test helpers to wrap `World` in `createCanvasWorldReadPort(world)` instead of passing concrete `World` to `CanvasPresentationSelector`.
    26	
    27	## Deletes / narrowing completed
    28	
    29	- Deleted `CanvasPresentationController.buildModel(world: World, ...)` full-World selector API.
    30	- Deleted `CanvasPresentationSelector.select(world: World, ...)` full-World selector API.
    31	- Deleted `CanvasPresentationSelector` active `any` seams (`item(primitive: any, kind: any)`, `Map<string, any>`, `world as any`, `(line as any).arcGeometry`).
    32	- Deleted direct projected-3D rendering loops from `CanvasPresentationSelector`; ownership is now `Projected3DCanvasSelector`.
    33	- Deleted obsolete concrete-World selector tests by replacing them with read-port/DTO tests.
    34	- Deleted mutable/spatial-query responsibilities from `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` after static scan showed active hit-testing ownership in `CanvasInteractionQuery` and no `new Paper(` / `class Paper` active usage remained.
    35	- No e2e workaround deletion was needed; current e2e already clicks canvas by test id. Overlay input ownership is now explicit and covered by live browser evidence.
    36	- No compatibility wrapper or dual full-World/read-port canvas selector path remains.
