    91	## Residual risks / future candidates
    92	
    93	- The `CanvasWorldReadPort` adapter still delegates some realization calls to the concrete runtime `World`; this is intentional for the bounded direct path and avoids broad domain/context restructuring. A future wave could introduce a domain-level realization read context if broader selector/3D traversal boundaries become central.
    94	- Existing tool unit tests still use local helper `any` parameters for mock `hitTest` functions; these are test-helper seams outside the decision-bound active presentation source. They were not broadened here.
    95	- Three.js `OrbitControls` still exists inside `ThreeSceneHost`; the overlay canvas is non-intercepting in the current app overlay so broad 3D scene interaction redesign remains deferred.
    96	
    97	## Next-wave recommendation / re-rank
    98	
    99	`architecture-audit/wave-plan.md` currently ends at Wave 016, so there is no already-authored Wave 017 entry to execute directly. Based on the Wave 016 learnings and the remaining residual risks above, the next canonical stage should be a fresh scout/proposal stage named `cycle-017-fresh-scout-proposals` whose first task is to re-read the current source tree and update `architecture-audit/wave-plan.md` with the next central wave before any implementation. Candidate central topics to evaluate, in order, are:
   100	
   101	1. Whether the remaining concrete-`World` realization delegation inside `CanvasWorldReadPort` should become a domain-level realization/read-context boundary.
   102	2. Whether remaining interaction/tool test-helper `any` seams indicate a broader typed interaction-query/test-fixture boundary worth cleaning.
   103	3. Whether any remaining 3D scene interaction ownership around `ThreeSceneHost`/`OrbitControls` is architectural debt now that overlay pointer ownership is explicit.
   104	
   105	No Wave 017 implementation was started during this closure task.
